WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.149
Data control is the foundation of sovereign AI.

2
00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:16.060
An AI workflow may process prompts, uploaded files, retrieved documents, embeddings, chat history, generated outputs, tool results, logs, telemetry, evaluation records, and user feedback.

3
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.107
Some of that data may be public.

4
00:00:18.107 --> 00:00:26.138
Some may be internal. Some may be confidential, regulated, customer-specific, personal, or operationally sensitive.

5
00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:31.491
A practical program starts by classifying the data that can enter each workflow.

6
00:00:31.491 --> 00:00:44.481
Teams should know whether prompts may include customer records, source code, contract language, incident details, credentials, health information, financial data, or proprietary strategy.

7
00:00:44.481 --> 00:00:47.315
They should also understand derived data.

8
00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:55.897
Embeddings, summaries, evaluations, and logs can carry sensitive meaning even when they do not look like the original document.

9
00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:59.125
Privacy boundaries can be broken accidentally.

10
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.667
Sensitive prompts may be routed to the wrong service.

11
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.636
Logs may be retained too long.

12
00:01:04.636 --> 00:01:07.785
Embeddings may be stored without a clear owner.

13
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:11.327
Retrieval systems may ignore document permissions.

14
00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:16.917
Monitoring data may be shared more broadly than the underlying content would allow.

15
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:21.405
These are design and operations problems, not only legal concerns.

16
00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:33.371
Sovereign AI needs explicit rules for what data can enter each workflow, where it can be stored, who can inspect it, how long it can be retained, and when it must be deleted or reviewed.

17
00:01:33.371 --> 00:01:38.252
Separate inference data from retrieval data and operational telemetry.

18
00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:41.244
Preserve tenant and permission boundaries.

19
00:01:41.244 --> 00:01:45.338
Use redaction and access control where logging is necessary.

20
00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:51.557
Strong data control makes later decisions about models, deployment, and policy much easier.
